# decoder_mp3.c/minimp3.h reference this directly (see decoder_cfg.h and
# tuya_mem_section.h), so it stays global rather than nested under
# ENABLE_AI_PLAYER's Decoder Options menu in src/audio_player/Kconfig; no other
# platform selects it.
config MP3_DECODER_STATIC_BUF
    bool "MP3_DECODER_STATIC_BUF: use static internal RAM for minimp3 scratch/context"
    default n
    help
      Place mp3dec_scratch_t, the decoder context and L12_scale_info in static
      buffers in TUYA_MEM_SECTION_RAM instead of allocating them per frame.

      This is about memory latency, not heap pressure. With ENABLE_EXT_RAM the
      MP3_MALLOC hook allocates from PSRAM, and decoding out of PSRAM cannot keep
      up: mp3dec_scratch_t (grbuf/syn, ~16KB) is read and written throughout every
      frame, which stutters audibly on SiWx917. Static internal RAM removes both
      the per-frame allocation and the PSRAM access latency.

      Costs ~24KB of internal RAM permanently and makes decoding non-reentrant,
      so enable it only for single-stream playback. The linker script must place
      the tuyaopen_bss_to_ram section (note: the section name has no leading dot).

